Subject: [PATCH] matrix-keypad: report presses as 1, releases as 0

The Rev C device tree marks the column, PTT and OPT GPIOs GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW, so
gpiod_get_value() already returns 1 while a key is pressed. The driver inverted
that once more, so every key reported 0 on press and 1 on release, and at load
every key was reported as pressed. Report the logical value instead: standard
evdev semantics for every reader (LVGL, raylib, linht-shelld). gui_test had
worked around the inversion (KEY_PRESS 0) and needs the matching change.

Upstream-Status: Pending [kept here until the LVGL Radio app replaces gui_test: upstream gui_test expects inverted keys, docs/architecture.md D30]
---
--- a/matrix-keypad.c
+++ b/matrix-keypad.c
@@ -65,8 +65,8 @@
         // udelay(1);
 
         for (c = 0; c < MATRIX_COLS; c++) {
-            // If a column reads low, the key is pressed
-            if (gpiod_get_value(data->col_gpios->desc[c]) == 0) {
+            // The DT marks the columns GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW: the logical value is 1 while the key is pressed
+            if (gpiod_get_value(data->col_gpios->desc[c])) {
                 current_key_state |= (1U << (r * MATRIX_COLS + c));
             }
         }
@@ -100,7 +100,7 @@
         ptt_now |= gpiod_get_value(data->ext_ptt_gpio);
 
     if (ptt_now != data->ptt_last) {
-        input_report_key(input_dev, KEY_P, !ptt_now);
+        input_report_key(input_dev, KEY_P, ptt_now);
         data->ptt_last = ptt_now;
         any_changed = true;
     }
@@ -109,7 +109,7 @@
     if (data->opt_gpio) {
         bool opt_now = gpiod_get_value(data->opt_gpio);
         if (opt_now != data->opt_last) {
-            input_report_key(input_dev, KEY_O, !opt_now);
+            input_report_key(input_dev, KEY_O, opt_now);
             data->opt_last = opt_now;
             any_changed = true;
         }
